{"type": "thinking", "text": "TOWER group: First Step (Clear your first Infinite Tower floor) not ✓, Tower Initiate (Reach floor 10) not ✓.\n\nInteresting! \"TOWER\" achievements are not obtained — but the precondition says \"Infinite Tower bonuses earned: +7% XP, +12% coin drops and +150 HP\". If tower floor 1 not cleared, how are bonuses earned? Contradiction! So tower achievements show no progress, suggesting the tower bonuses are NOT from floor milestones. Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe the Infinite Tower bonuses are a different mechanism: \"Infinite Tower bonuses earned: +7% XP, +12% coin drops, +150 HP\" might be from the tower's \"milestones\" screen (Floor 10 reward Tower Ring, Floor 20 +1% XP...) — but if no floor cleared, none.\n\nHmm, so where do +7% XP, +12% coins, +150 HP come from? Maybe from the Gloomharvest event? Or from the \"Grand Monument\" (Gilded gives +10% coin drops)? Or from Prestige? Hmm.\n\n+150 HP: maybe from Vitality prestige? No, that's +4.\n\nMaybe from \"Infinite Tower\" permanent bonuses displayed somewhere else (e.g., in the tower screen's top: \"Floor 1\"??). Actually maybe the tower screen top shows current floor=1 but the \"Infinite Tower bonuses\" are from an event/building.\n\nHmm, wait: the Grand Monument \"Gilded\" gives +10% coin drops. Not 12%.\n\nCould the +7% XP / +12% coins / +150 HP be from \"Infinite Tower\" rewards accumulated over floors 1-? (e.g., each floor gives some bonus). The tower screen milestones (Floor 10, 20...) show rewards: Floor 20 = +1% tower XP all skills; Floor 60 = +50 max HP. But those are locked.\n\nHmm, maybe the sweep data's \"Infinite Tower bonuses earned\" are actually values that should appear in the Profile bonuses section regardless of the tower screen's current run floor. The tower \"current floor\" may reset per run, but best floor persists — the achievements should be unlocked then. Hmm, but achievements \"Clear your first Infinite Tower floor\" is locked, so no floors cleared.\n\nThis is confusing; the precondition data might be intentionally inconsistent with the app state? Hmm, that's odd for a QA task. Unless the milestone/achievement progress is buggy — which is exactly what the changed item is about: \"progress toward mission milestones is now computed from all finished progress records.\" Maybe the tower achievements are \"mission milestones\" and their progress is computed wrong → they show as locked even though floors were finished. Hmm! But the \"Profile milestones section\" wording...\n\nOhh! Maybe \"mission milestones\" is the term for these achievement-like \"MILESTONES\" in the **Tower**?? Hmm.\n\nWait, actually, maybe the app has \"Milestones\" section in the \"Profile\" → \"Achievements\"? The achievements are grouped into categories; maybe the app internally calls achievements \"milestones\"? Hmm.\n\nAlternatively, maybe \"Infinite Tower bonuses earned\" are stored in the profile \"Bonuses\" section's global bonuses, and the fact that achievements show locked is fine because the bonuses are separate.\n\nLet me look at the tower screen again: maybe there are \"earned bonuses\" shown at the top or in a section, e.g., \"Earned bonuses: +7% XP, +12% coins, +150 HP\". The tower screen showed Floor 1, Weapon, Attempt Floor 1, Debug Advance Floor, Milestones list. Hmm, no earned bonuses section visible. Maybe scrolling down the tower screen shows \"Earned Bonuses\"! The tower screen is scrollable (milestones list). Let me scroll the tower screen to see if there's a \"Bonuses\" section.\n\nActually let me reconsider the whole task. The four changed items:\n1. Profile milestones section — progress toward mission milestones computed from all finished progress records.\n2. Skill training XP bar — relative to start of current level.\n3. Skill training action list — ordered by required level.\n4. Profile bonuses section — listed bonuses from a new set of sources.\n\nMaybe the app is not the same as I assume; maybe \"missions\" = \"Acts\"/\"Chapters\"? Hmm.\n\nLet me search for the word \"Milestone\" in the app by checking the \"Church\", \"Inn\", \"Shop\", \"Builder's Workshop\" - maybe one of them has \"Milestones\". But \"Profile milestones section\" specifically.\n\nWAIT. Maybe the Profile screen has a \"Milestones\" section that appears only when no sidebar item content... no, sidebar always has one selected.\n\nHmm, but hold on: maybe the \"Milestones\" section is in the **Skill Tree** screen (per skill)! The skill tree has nodes (\"XP Boost\", \"Purer Ore\"...). No.\n\nOr maybe in the \"Expeditions\" screen: each expedition has \"0 / 5 lore notes\" — milestones? Hmm, \"progress toward mission milestones computed from all finished progress records\": Expeditions are literally \"missions\"; each has milestones as lore notes discovered. The expedition card shows \"0 / 5 lore notes\" progress. If progress records (finished explorations) exist, the count should be >0. The preconditions don't mention expeditions, so 0/5 is plausible.\n\nI think I need to accept that the \"profile milestones section\" may not be discoverable by label; maybe it's the \"Achievements\" screen (with progress toward mission milestones = achievements?). Hmm.\n\nHold on, let me reconsider the phrase \"mission milestones\". In many idle games, \"Missions\" are a system with milestones. In this app, maybe \"Quests\" are called \"missions\"? The Quests completed precondition (Mining I etc.) suggests quests. The achievements \"QUESTS\" group has \"Complete 5 quests\" etc. Those are arguably \"mission milestones\" and they're computed from quest completion progress records! The Achievements screen is part of the Profile. So \"Profile milestones section\" might mean the **Achievements section**?? Hmm, but it says \"milestones section\" not \"achievements\".\n\nAlternatively \"Profile milestones\" could be the achievements' \"progress toward mission milestones\" — e.g., the \"Quest Hound: Complete 25 quests\" should show progress (e.g., \"7 / 25\") when incomplete. In the Missing view, incomplete achievements show only the description without progress numbers. Maybe the new build was supposed to add progress under each achievement (like \"7 / 25\")! And the fact it's missing could be the bug. Hmm, but the change note says \"progress toward mission milestones is now computed from all finished progress records\", which might refer to a number displayed somewhere.\n\nHmm, hmm. Let me look at the Achievements screen's Incomplete items again: no numeric progress. But perhaps tapping an achievement opens a detail with progress. Let me tap an incomplete achievement (e.g., Master) and see if a detail sheet shows progress. That might reveal the \"milestones\" section!\n\nLet me try tapping \"Master\" in the Achievements list. But we're at TOWER group in All view. Let me scroll back up or use the Missing filter. Actually, let's tap \"Tower Initiate\" (incomplete) at (590,1986)."}
