g—Stone queued.\n- Crafting 20: 4,470 / 5,018 = 0.0 (start of level 20 = 4,470 ✓).\n- Farming 1: 0/83 (level 1 start 0, level2 83 ✓)\n- Fletching 1: 0/83.\n\nNow the XP bar progress for Smithing 19 = 0.85915494. Expected (4400-3973)/(4470-3973) = 427/497 = 0.85915494... EXACTLY. So the row's progress bar is correct relative to level start. Good.\n\nHmm, but maybe the bug is in the training screen's bar — which we haven't located. Maybe the row progress uses the correct formula while the training sheet's bar uses a different one. Since there's no bar in the Choose Activity sheet, maybe the \"skill training XP bar\" is in the Choose Activity sheet but only for skills with actions? For Mining we saw no bar. Hmm.\n\nWait! Maybe the Choose Activity sheet's header bar is present but rendered as a thin line under the \"Session: 56m\"? Not in the tree. Hmm.\n\nAlternatively, the \"skill training screen\" could be the screen you get by tapping a skill in the **Profile → Skills** tile: the sheet showed \"Mining / Level 50 / Prestige / View tree\" then the action list. No bar either. Hmm, but wait: maybe the bar is the circular... no.\n\nHmm, maybe the XP bar is in the **Skills tab row** after all, and the change note refers to those rows. But we verified it's correct for Smithing. Let me check other rows' progress values for consistency:\n- Attack 70: 737,627/814,445 → 0.0. Level 70 start = 737,627 ✓ → 0.\n- Ranged 40: 37,224/41,171 → 0.0 ✓ (level 40 start 37,224).\n- HP 70: 0.0 ✓.\n- Mercantile 99: ring fully gold? Mercantile level 99 with unknown XP — probably at level 99 start? The ring in the screenshot was fully gold (complete). Hmm, at level 99 the bar could be full if XP is at max? Hmm.\n\nSo all bars seem right. Unless there's a case where a skill's XP is mid-level and the bar shows wrong. Smithing is that case and it's right.\n\nHmm, then the XP bar bug might be elsewhere: maybe in the Choose Activity sheet when a session is queued? Or the \"Home session card\" percentage \"Lv 50 (6%)\": +720 XP from 101,333 to 102,053 = 720/10,612 = 6.78% → displayed 6% (truncated). Reasonable.\n\nHmm, maybe the XP bar is in the \"Skill Tree\" screen? No.\n\nWait — maybe the \"skill training screens\" refer to **Combat training screens** (dungeon sessions) which have XP bars per skill? Hmm.\n\nLet me look at the \"Skills (1)\" tab: maybe tapping \"Expeditions\" etc. Hmm.\n\nCould the \"skill training screen\" be the sheet we saw in Profile→Skills tile: \"Mining, Level 50, Prestige, View tree, [list of actions with Lv and ✓]\" — that's the \"skill training action list\" perhaps! And the XP bar might be the row bar under \"Mining\" in that sheet? The sheet had no bar. Hmm, but wait: the sheet elements list showed \"View desc=Close sheet, Drag handle, Mining, Level 50, Prestige, View tree...\" — the level 50 text; maybe a bar exists as a non-accessible View (like the gold ring images). Hmm.\n\nLet me look at the screenshot of the Skills tab list to see where bars are and confirm the bars. Also check the Cooking row anomaly (clock + \" ..\") which may indicate something.\n\nLet me go to Skills tab and screenshot."}
