eah.\n\nOK, maybe the \"skill training screen\" is the Choose Activity sheet and the XP bar is at the very top of the sheet *above the title*, and is only a few pixels tall (partially hidden under the drag handle)? In the Mining sheet, elements began with \"Drag handle\" at y=63 — a bar above could be hidden behind the status bar. Hmm.\n\nHonestly, I've verified the XP bar in the Skills tab is correct. But maybe the injected bug is that the XP bar there is correct while the *XP text* is wrong? Let's examine the XP display text carefully: \"4,400 / 4,470 XP\" for Smithing 19. If the bar is level-relative, the text should ideally be \"427 / 497 XP\" (XP into level / XP needed). The change note says only progress (bar) changed. The text still shows absolute XP values, which is arguably intentional.\n\nHmm, but here's a thought: what if the intended fix (per change note) is that the bar should be relative to level start, and the BUG is that the *text* uses the same relative values but the bar uses absolute? We see the bar is relative and the text absolute. So no bug.\n\nWait, maybe I should test a *different* screen: the Choose Activity sheet for a skill shows \"+720 XP → Level 51\" etc. Hmm, those previews are computed relative to level? For Mining: +720 XP from 101,333 → 102,053, still level 50, so no level-up arrow (the Mining sheet earlier showed no \"→ Level\" for those, consistent).\n\nHmm, what about the \"→ Level 31\" for Fishing? +1,800 from 13,363 = 15,163; level 31 (needs 14,833). So it displays \"→ Level 31\" ✓. If it were computed as total XP vs thresholds it'd be the same. Hmm.\n\nOK, let me look at the \"skills (1)\" tab's info icon (element 15 \"Quest icons\" at top right). Maybe tapping it opens a \"Skill training info/XP\" panel. Hmm.\n\nActually, maybe the \"skill training screen\" is the **\"Skill Tree\"** screen? No.\n\nCould the \"training screen\" be accessed via the \"i\" info button on Skills tab? Let me tap it."}
