r than a screen. The note could be describing internal logic: \"Profile milestones section\" might be a data field in the profile (player save) for milestone progress. Hmm!\n\nActually yes!! In many apps, \"profile\" refers to the player's saved profile object, not the UI screen. The note \"Profile milestones section: progress toward mission milestones is now computed from all finished progress records\" likely means the *player profile's milestones* feature — which could be the Tower Milestones / Achievements. The \"profile screen\" might be the screen showing the profile... Hmm, but the QA task says areas are \"the profile screen\" and \"the skill training screens\".\n\nGiven the ambiguity, I should test the Infinite Tower Milestones since that's the only \"Milestones\" section in the app! And its state conflicts with the precondition (tower bonuses earned). Let me examine it more:\n\nTower screen: \"Floor 1\" and \"Weapon: Iron Sword (Attack)\", \"Attempt Floor 1\", \"Debug Advance floor\", \"Milestones\" list with Floor 10..130+.\n\nPrecondition: \"Infinite Tower bonuses earned: +7% XP, +12% coin drops and +150 HP.\" The milestones rewards include \"+1% tower XP all skills\" (floor 20), \"+1% tower coin drops\" (floor 110), \"+50 max HP\" (floor 60). To have +7% XP, you'd need floors 20+70+... etc.\n\nMaybe the earned bonuses are a *summary* shown in the profile bonuses. If the profile bonuses showed those, we'd see +7% XP, +12% coin drops, +150 HP. Not present → bug in bonuses section. And the tower milestone claims are independent (unclaimed because... hmm).\n\nOK. Decision: report the missing Infinite Tower bonuses from Profile→Bonuses. That's consistent with the changed item #4 and the precondition data.\n\nNow, since #1 \"profile milestones\" remains unfound, maybe the \"Milestones\" section is indeed the *Infinite Tower's* and the \"profile\" in the note refers to it. Let me test the tower milestone progress by using the \"[Debug] Advance floor\" to see if