ithing / Only craftable / toggle / description / Quests / Skill Tree / filters / items\". No bar. So no.\n\nOK, decision: The XP bar = Skills tab row bar, verified correct. So no bug there in my view. Hmm, but the benchmark expects a bug in each changed item? Not necessarily — changed items could be fixes that are correct.\n\nMaybe the actual injected bugs are:\n1. Bonus section missing tower bonuses (likely).\n2. Milestones progress wrong somewhere (unfound).\n3. XP bar wrong somewhere (unfound).\n4. Ordering wrong somewhere (unfound).\n\nAlternatively, maybe I'm wrong about the XP bar: Let me examine the bar on the Skills row more carefully by measuring pixels for a mid-level skill. Let's compute from the screenshot: Smithing row bar at preview y≈1197, from x≈159 to x≈865 (width 706). Fill ended at x≈768. Fill fraction = (768-159)/706 = 0.862 ≈ 0.859 ✓. So correct.\n\nOK so where's the bug?! Maybe the XP bar is *also* displayed in the Choose Activity sheet as a bar under the \"Session: 56m\" line, and it's actually there but rendered as a *thin 2px line* which is hard to distinguish. Hmm, no.\n\nLet me look at the Fishing sheet again: the line at y≈722 in preview spanning x=23..878. In the Mining screenshot earlier, there was a similar line at y≈505. Both likely dividers.\n\nAlright, maybe the \"skill training screens\" refers to the **Combat** training screens (dungeon session screens). Let me look at a dungeon's training screen: Combat → Dungeons → Farm. Tapping Farm opens a sheet with activities? Let me check. A combat training screen might show a combat XP bar and an action list (monsters) ordered by level! That could be the actual \"skill training screens\" — the combat ones. Let me check Farm."}
