{"type": "thinking", "text": "Confirmed Fishing sheet: no \"~60 fish/session\" line. And the sheet header lacks the skill title/level (\"Fishing\" at top) that Smithing had (\"Smithing\" title) — Mining's sheet had \"Choose Activity\" as title too. Hmm, Smithing's sheet had \"Smithing\" + \"Only craftable\" toggle as title row. So gathering sheets have \"Choose Activity\" title; crafting sheets have skill name + toggle. Fine.\n\nWait, the Fishing sheet lacks the skill name in the header? Mining's sheet also had only \"Choose Activity\" + description. So consistent.\n\nSo the missing \"~N fish/session\" line for Fishing/Woodcutting may be a bug, but is it in the changes? Not listed. Hmm.\n\nHmm, one more important observation: The Fishing action rows show \"+300 XP\", \"+600 XP\", \"+900 XP\", \"+1,200 XP\", \"+1,800 XP → Level 31\", \"+2,700 XP → Level 31\". Earlier before the session was active, the Mining rows showed \"+900 XP\" etc. AND the header had \"~60 ores/session\". So the XP amounts equal 60 × XP/catch. For Fishing: 60 × 5 = 300 ✓; 60×10=600 ✓; 60×15=900 ✓; 60×20=1200 ✓; 60×30=1800 ✓; 60×45=2700 ✓. Good.\n\nSo for Fishing, the per-session yield exists implicitly (60). The missing \"~60 fish/session\" label is just informational.\n\nHmm! Wait. What about the XP bar? The rows show \"+1,800 XP → Level 31\" — \"→ Level 31\" for a session from level 30. Now, the Fishing skill's XP bar in the Skills tab shows 0% (13,363/14,833). After the session (+2,700 XP → 16,063), the bar should be (16,063-14,833)/(16,456-14,833) = 1,230/1,623 = 75.8%. But the preview says \"→ Level 31\" only. Fine.\n\nOK, I've got to make decisions. Given the uncertainty, let me look at the *Choose Activity* sheet title for Cooking/Fletching etc. Not needed.\n\nLet me now try to find the \"profile milestones\" by checking the *Banners* section content (maybe milestones per event?) and the *Notes* (no). Hmm.\n\nActually, WAIT! Let me re-read the Changed list once more:\n- \"Profile milestones section: progress toward mission milestones is now computed from all finished progress records.\"\n\nWhat if \"mission milestones\" refers to the **Infinite Tower Milestones** which are the rewards you claim (\"Claim all 25 tower milestones\")? The \"profile\" might be the *player profile data* where milestones are stored. And the changed section is the Infinite Tower's \"Milestones\" section! The phrase \"mission milestones\" might be a typo for \"tower milestones\" — Hmm, but \"progress toward...\" The tower Milestones show buttons with floor requirements, and progress is the highest floor. With the precondition's earned bonuses, the highest floor should be high and many milestones claimed.\n\nThe tower screen shows \"Floor 1\" (current), and all milestone buttons disabled. Hmm, but the precondition's \"Infinite Tower bonuses earned\" says the player HAS earned +7% XP etc. So the milestone progress should show. But it doesn't, and neither do achievements. This looks like a real inconsistency. However, maybe the bonuses were earned in a prior *season* and reset? Hmm, the tower's milestone claim state would persist.\n\nHmm, hmm, this is risky to report without clear expected UI.\n\nAlternative: maybe the \"profile milestones\" section is the **\"Pets\"** screen's \"0 / 30 obtained\" progress? No.\n\nHmm, hold on! Let me reconsider \"mission milestones\" – maybe the app has \"Missions\" in the **Carnival** (Idle Games)? No.\n\nLet me check the *Inn* and *Church* quickly to look for \"Milestones\": Inn might have \"rest milestones\"? Church blessings? Hmm, unlikely.\n\nWait, what about the \"Armory\" screen? It's a collection (16/367). No.\n\nWhat about \"Bestiary\" (0/100)? no.\n\nSo the only literal \"Milestones\" is the Infinite Tower. Therefore, I'll treat the Infinite Tower Milestones as the \"milestones section\" (the only candidate) and test its progress. The precondition's tower bonuses are the ground truth for progress. The milestones list should reflect floors reached (e.g., Floor 10 claimed, etc.). Currently all disabled + \"Floor 1\". That contradicts earned bonuses. But wait — the earned bonuses might be from milestones NOT tied to floors: the milestone rewards list includes \"Tower Ring (attack +6, strength +6)\", \"+1% tower XP all skills\", \"5,000 coins\", etc. The +7% XP / +12% coin drops / +150 HP could be the *aggregate* of many claimed milestones (e.g., +1% XP × 7 = floors 20,70,...; +1% coins ×12; +50 HP ×3). For +7% XP, you'd need floor 20 (+1%), 70 (+2%), 120? (+?), etc. To get +12% coins, twelve +1% coin milestones. That means floors up to ~300+. The achievements \"Reach floor 250\" (Void Conqueror) would be unlocked then. It's not. So the tower state is definitely inconsistent with the earned bonuses.\n\nGiven the instruction \"Use the starting data described in the preconditions in your tests\", the data is ground truth. So the tower milestone progress being zero is a bug. But which report screen? \"Infinite Tower\" screen. However, the task areas are profile + skill training. Reporting an Infinite Tower bug may be out of scope...\n\nHmm, maybe the sweep's \"profile milestones section\" IS this: the Infinite Tower milestone progress is stored in the profile (player data). The note says \"progress toward mission milestones is now computed from all finished progress records\". Hmm, \"finished progress records\" — in the tower context, each floor attempt is a \"progress record\". So the milestone progress should be computed from finished floor records. If the player has earned +7% XP etc., the milestone progress is broken (shows 0/floor 1). Hmm!\n\nBut the tower milestone buttons show *no progress numbers*, just disabled. So the visible symptom: milestones all locked even though tower bonuses are earned. Hmm, this might indeed be the injected bug for item #1! But it's labeled \"profile milestones\" — maybe the tower milestone display is on the *Combat/Infinite Tower* screen, not profile. Hmm.\n\nUgh. Let me look at the tower again: is there a \"Milestones\" section in the Profile? NO. The tower has it. The sweep area says \"the profile screen\" and \"the skill training screens\". The changed items include \"Profile milestones section\". If the bug were in the tower, the sweep area would include the tower. So the milestones must be in the Profile screen... but there is none!\n\nUNLESS: the \"Profile\" screen in \"Tabs\" layout has a tab I haven't seen because the tab row scroll was at the end... The Tabs layout tabs were: Inventory, Gear, Pets, Achievements, Notes, Bestiary, Armory. Hmm, maybe there are more tabs to the LEFT of Inventory — we swiped right and it stopped at Inventory. Unless the row has a \"Skills\" tab that is *not* rendered because... hmm.\n\nWait, actually — maybe in Tabs layout, \"Skills\" IS the first tab but we can't scroll further right because the row is at its start... and the leftmost visible tab is Inventory because the row's content is scrolled such that Inventory starts at x=108 with some left padding, and \"Skills\" doesn't exist. So no.\n\nHmm, hold on: what if the Tabs layout's sections are: Skills, Inventory, Gear, Pets, Achievements, Notes, Bestiary, Armory, Bonuses, Banners — and the visible portion starts mid-list because the *selected* tab (Pets) is scrolled into view. Our right swipe should reveal earlier tabs. It revealed Inventory as leftmost. That suggests Skills is absent... Hmm, OR the swipe right didn't fully reach the start (maybe the row only scrolls when the touch starts on a tab; our swipe at y=558 is on the tab row, fine). It moved from Inventory(93)->Gear(304)... wait, in the first Tabs observation after switching, Inventory was at 93. Then after swiping left twice, tabs shifted left. Then I swiped right 0.6 and Inventory appeared at 108 (slightly right of 93) — so that's the start. So no Skills tab.\n\nSo in Tabs layout, Skills/Bonuses/Banners are missing. Interesting. Maybe the Tabs layout is intended to only have those 7? Weird.\n\nOK, alternative hypothesis: The \"profile milestones section\" could be the *\"Achievements\"* section, which is present in both layouts. And the \"progress toward mission milestones\" = the \"13/38\" count computed from progress records. We verified 13/38 matches the state including quest records. Hmm, except maybe it should be 14/", "truncated": true}
