{"type": "thinking", "text": "Banners: two banners unobtained. No milestones.\n\nOK. Let me now think about \"Infinite Tower bonuses earned\" differently: maybe the \"Infinite Tower bonuses\" are stored in the **Bonuses** section and should show as \"+7% XP\", \"+12% coins\", \"+150 HP\" — and their absence is THE bug for item #4. I'll report that.\n\nFor item #1 \"Profile milestones section\", maybe the section is the *Achievements* progress \"13/38 34%\"... OR the *Tower milestones*. Hmm, the wording \"progress toward mission milestones is now computed from all finished progress records\" —\n\nWAIT. Maybe \"mission\" here = \"**Infinite Tower runs are called 'missions'**\"? Hmm.\n\nAlternatively — maybe \"mission milestones\" refers to **guild milestones** (\"Complete 0/2 daily requests to advance\"). The Guild Hall detail shows \"Level 0 / ProgressBar 0.0 / 0 / 2 dailies / Complete 0/2 daily requests to advance\". That IS progress toward a milestone (guild level advancement) and it's computed from *finished daily-request progress records*. With 3 guild quests completed (per precondition), but these are *quests*, not daily requests. Hmm, \"0/2 dailies\" seems consistent since daily requests are 0/300.\n\nBUT the guild level shows 0 and the guild list shows \"Mining Guild Level 0 4 left today\". Hmm.\n\nAlternatively the \"profile milestones section\" could be the **Guild Hall's** level progress? Not profile.\n\nHmm, hold on. Let me re-read the precondition: \"Quests completed: Mining I, Fishing I, Woodcutting I and Smithing I, plus the guild quests Copper Run, Iron Quota and Shrimp Haul (3 guild quests).\" This data is likely given specifically for the \"milestones\" test — i.e., some milestone progress is based on ALL quests including guild quests. E.g., an achievement/milestone \"Complete 5 quests\" should count guild quests too (\"all finished progress records\"). And indeed \"Dedicated (Complete 5 quests)\" is ✓ — which requires counting guild quests (4 skill quests + 3 guild = 7) OR just the 4 skill quests wouldn't reach 5. So the \"Dedicated\" achievement ✓ requires counting all 7 progress records. That's consistent with \"progress toward mission milestones is now computed from all finished progress records\"!!\n\nSo the \"Profile milestones section\" = the **Achievements** (milestones)? Specifically the achievements that count quests! Hmm, but achievements are \"achievements\"...\n\nHmm, wait: maybe there's a *separate* \"Milestones\" concept on the profile: the \"Achievements\" screen's progress? The change note: \"Profile milestones section: progress toward mission milestones...\" Perhaps the app calls the achievements \"milestones\" internally (the IDs might be \"milestones\"). The Achievements section shows \"13 / 38 obtained\" and individual achievements like \"Complete 25 quests\". The \"progress toward mission milestones\" would be the *obtained* state of mission-related achievements computed from progress records. \"Dedicated (Complete 5 quests)\" ✓ and \"Quester (Complete 1 quest)\" ✓ — consistent with all records (4+3=7).\n\nHmm, so maybe the bug is that some achievement that should be ✓ isn't. Let's check: with 7 completed quests, \"Quest Hound (Complete 25 quests)\" ✗ correct. \"Quester\" ✓, \"Dedicated\" ✓. Hmm.\n\nWhat else could \"progress toward mission milestones\" affect? Maybe the \"COLLECTION\" or \"TOWN\" achievements? Hmm.\n\nHmm, maybe the milestones progress is the **\"Tower Legend: Claim all 25 tower milestones\"** — achievements based on \"milestones\" progress. The tower milestones ARE \"milestones\" and their progress is computed from finished floor records. The precondition says tower bonuses earned → many milestones claimed → \"Tower Legend\" should be ✓ (if all 25) or at least some tower achievements ✓. They're all ✗ and the tower screen shows Floor 1 with 0 claimed. So the milestone progress is NOT computed from finished progress records (the earned bonuses prove records exist). This matches \"progress toward mission milestones is now computed from all finished progress records\" being broken!\n\nBut the \"Profile milestones section\"... The Achievements are in the Profile. The tower milestone progress affects the Profile's Achievements (TOWER group). Hmm, plausible!\n\nHmm, but the tower screen itself also shows milestones. If the player has claimed 25 milestones, they'd show as claimed. They don't. So the underlying data (tower milestone claims) seems absent, not just the progress computation. Unless the bonuses were granted directly without milestones.\n\nUgh.\n\nOK, let me weigh: the most defensible, concrete bugs with on-screen evidence and precondition ground truth:\n\nA) Bonuses section missing Infinite Tower bonuses (+7% XP, +12% coin drops, +150 HP). Ground truth: precondition says earned. Evidence: Bonuses list has only 5 entries. — Report.\n\nB) Infinite Tower milestones show all locked / Floor 1 despite earned tower bonuses (+7% XP/+12% coin drops/+150 HP), and achievements TOWER group all uncompleted. Ground truth: precondition. Evidence: tower screen \"Floor 1\" + disabled milestone buttons. — Could report, but out of stated sweep areas; however \"profile milestones\" might be this. Hmm, the tower is not profile.\n\nC) Tabs layout missing Skills/Bonuses/Banners sections. Evidence: tab row ends at Armory. Ground truth: rail layout has them; a layout setting shouldn't remove sections. — Could report as missing/consistency bug on the profile screen. This is within the profile area. But is it a \"new build\" change? Not listed. Hmm. It might be intentional (Tabs layout intentionally excludes some?). Risky but plausible bug.\n\nHmm, wait. Actually, let me double check C: maybe the tab row in Tabs layout DID include Skills but the row was originally scrolled to make the selected tab (Pets) visible, and my right-swipe only scrolled partially because the row is 5 tabs wide... Let me re-examine: after switching to Tabs, the tab items were Inventory(93), Gear(304), Pets(540), Achievements(816), Notes(1027). If Skills existed, it would be left of Inventory; since the row can scroll, the initial position could center Pets. My right swipe (finger moves right = content moves right = reveal earlier) at distance 0.6 from x=500; result Inventory(108), Gear(334), Pets(570)... That's a shift of ~20px only, not to the start! Hmm, the tab row moved right by only ~15-30px! So maybe it hit the beginning (Inventory at 108 with padding). But if the row had a \"Skills\" tab, the beginning would show Skills at ~90. It shows Inventory at 108. So inventory is first.\n\nHmm, could it be that the row's start is Inventory because the *Skills* tab is intentionally omitted in tabs mode (since Skills is in the bottom nav)? That seems intentional design! Yes — in Tabs mode, \"Skills\" might be omitted because there's already a Skills tab in the bottom nav. That's plausible design. So not a bug.\n\nBut Bonuses/Banners missing from Tabs mode is still odd... Maybe those are intentionally not included? Hmm. Actually wait, maybe the tabs row includes more items after Armory but scroll didn't reveal because the row's content ends at Armory. We saw: after two left swipes, Pets(2), Achievements(243), Notes(520), Bestiary(756), Armory(977) — the Armory tab at 977 is fully visible. A third swipe left did nothing. So Armory is last. So Bonuses/Banners absent in Tabs mode. Could be intentional? Unlikely — Bonuses is a fairly important section. Hmm.\n\nRisky but this is a real inconsistency between layouts. However, maybe the app's Tabs layout is *deliberately* limited to 7 sections and Bonuses/Banners are Rail-only. We can't know.\n\nLet me consider reporting the most likely \"designed\" bugs from the change list. Since I can't find a milestones section in Profile, maybe the section is literally missing (removed?) — but the change note says it's \"now computed\", implying it exists.\n\nHmm hold on, wait. Maybe the \"Profile milestones section\" is in the *Combined* profile header: Did I scroll the profile header in rail mode? The header is fixed. Hmm.\n\nLet me try one more thing: maybe the Profile screen in rail mode has a \"Milestones\" section *inside the \"Skills\" content* above the grid — the content area top had \"GATHERING\" heading. No.\n\nCould the \"Milestones\"", "truncated": true}
