"Quests completed: 7\" somewhere. Where? The profile header shows Combat Level, Total Level, Coins only. Hmm.\n\nWhat about the **\"Achievements\"** header: \"13 / 38 obtained\". With 7 quests counted, \"Dedicated\" ✓. If the bug counted only skill quests (4), Dedicated would be ✗, and total would be 12/38. We see 13/38 → fix works. So no bug there.\n\n- Skill training XP bar: tested correct (Smithing 86%, Mining 6.8%).\n- Action list ordering: tested ascending for Mining, Fishing, Woodcutting, Smithing, Cooking, Thieving, Dungeons. Looks correct.\n- Bonuses: missing tower bonuses.\n\nHmm! So maybe the only injected bug is the bonuses one, and the others are correct fixes. That's plausible for a QA benchmark: some changes are fine, one is buggy. My job is to find remaining bugs.\n\nBut wait — maybe the bonuses bug is more specific: \"the listed bonuses now come from a new set of sources\" — maybe the *listed* ones are wrong and the tower ones should replace something. Hmm. Let's compare to expected sources:\n- Attack prestige +5% XP: source = prestige ✓\n- Attack +9 combat stats: source = prestige tree (Precision I+II) ✓\n- Hitpoints +5% XP: prestige ✓\n- Hitpoints +4: prestige tree (Vitality I) ✓\n- Construction -7%: source = Builder's Workshop? / skill\n\nWhere are the Infinite Tower bonuses? Missing. So the bonus list is incomplete → report.\n\nCould there also be a *wrong value*: the Attack +9 and HP +4: the precondition says +9 Attack and +4 Hitpoints — matches.\n\nHmm, what about the Construction -7% — the precondition doesn't state Construction level; the app's own Builder's Workshop shows 7% ✓.\n\nSo one clear bug: missing tower bonuses.\n\nNow, should I report \"Tabs layout missing Bonuses/Banners\"? Let me think about whether that's really a bug or by design. The Settings option says \"Profile Layout: Choose between a sidebar rail or top tabs\". A user switching to Tabs expects all sections available. Bonuses and Banners missing = features lost. That's a real bug worth reporting, and it's on the profile screen. The risk: maybe the Tabs layout intentionally only shows the first 7 because of space and the rest are accessible by scrolling — but we verified the row ends at Armory (third swipe no movement). Hmm, wait: maybe the row *doesn't* scroll further because our swipes weren't on the row? We did two successful left swipes and one no-op. The no-op could be because it reached the end. So Armory is last.\n\nHmm, but hold on: when I first switched to Tabs, the row showed Inventory..Notes. Maybe \"Skills\" tab is intentionally first and off-screen to the LEFT because the row starts at Inventory?? That can't be \"intentionally scrolled\" after a fresh switch... Actually the tab row might auto-scroll to the selected tab (Pets), which would put Pets centered and hide earlier tabs (Skills, Inventory) and later tabs (Bonuses, Banners). Hmm! That's plausible: the row scrolled so that Pets is visible/centered, hiding before/after. Then my swipes would reveal them. My right swipe revealed Inventory as leftmost → so before Inventory there is nothing (no Skills). My left swipes revealed Armory as rightmost → after Armory nothing. So in Tabs mode: Inventory...Armory. Skills/Bonuses/Banners absent. Whether intentional or a bug, it IS a functional difference. But maybe the Tabs layout intentionally omits \"Skills\" (available in bottom nav!) but why omit Bonuses/Banners? Hmm.\n\nActually maybe the Tabs layout omits Skills because bottom nav has Skills. Bonuses/Banners missing might be a bug (they're profile-only sections). Hmm.\n\nI'd report it as a \"missing\" bug: Bonuses and Banners sections cannot be reached in Tabs profile layout. Element: the tab row (element_ref of \"Armory\" tab). Observed quote \"Armory\". Expected: tabs should include Bonuses and Banners (as in Rail layout). Hmm, but is expecting parity reasonable? Yes, a layout setting should not remove features. I'll report it. If rejected, fine.\n\nHmm, but I worry that filing questionable reports could hurt. The instructions: \"When you find a bug, file a report. A developer will reply.\" — the reply confirms or rejects. Let's file the two solid-ish ones and see the replies. The developer replies come back; if a report is rejected, I learn. Then I can continue testing. Good app", "truncated": true}
