{"type": "thinking", "text": "Smithing I \"Smelt 500 Bronze Bars\" — no \"Completed\" marker! But the precondition says Smithing I is completed. Hmm!! Interesting. In the Gathering tab, Fishing I/Mining I/Woodcutting I showed \"Completed\" + Reset. In Crafting Skills, Smithing I shows no Completed marker and no progress either. That's a discrepancy: the quest completion record exists (precondition) but the quest UI doesn't show it as completed.\n\nHmm, but maybe the quest list shows progress only when... hmm. Also note none of the crafting quests show progress bars at all (no \"0/500\"), unlike the Gathering tab which also didn't show progress bars for incomplete ones (only \"Completed\" for completed). In Gathering, incomplete quests (Fishing II, Mining II, Thieving I) showed no progress either. So quests for skill chains only show \"Completed\" when done, no progress otherwise. So Smithing I should show \"Completed\" if it's completed.\n\nThis is a potential bug: Smithing I is completed (per precondition) but not shown as completed in Quests → Crafting Skills. However, the precondition is data given to us; the app's saved state should reflect it. If the quest UI doesn't show Completed and the Reset button, then either the data isn't there or the UI is wrong.\n\nWait, maybe Smithing I was completed and *reset*? The \"Reset\" button on completed quests allows replay? If reset, it wouldn't be completed. Hmm.\n\nHmm, also: the \"Dedicated (Complete 5 quests)\" achievement ✓ requires ≥5 completed quests. We have Fishing I, Mining I, Woodcutting I, Smithing I (4) + guild quests (3). If Smithing I isn't actually completed, then Dedicated ✓ (with 5) implies guild quests counted (2+ of them). Copper Run completed ✓, Shrimp Haul?, Iron Quota ✗ (requires guild level 1). Hmm.\n\nThis suggests the \"all finished progress records\" includes guild quests, and it's working.\n\nBut the Smithing I display issue: is this within my areas? No (Quests is not profile or training). And maybe Smithing I is not completed in the actual state (precondition mismatch). Hmm, the precondition is supposed to be the state. I could report it, but it's out of the sweep areas... Actually \"Quests\" isn't in my areas. The instructions say sweep the profile and skill training screens. I should not go too far afield.\n\nLet me refocus: within the profile screen, the Achievements module is the \"milestones\" candidate. In the Achievements QUESTS group, \"Dedicated: Complete 5 quests\" ✓ — if Smithing I isn't counted, that's inconsistent with the precondition... but I can't verify.\n\nHmm hold on, actually: the change note says \"progress toward mission milestones is now computed from all finished progress records.\" Maybe \"mission milestones\" = the *Achievements* in the profile, and they're computed from progress records (quest/resource records). The seeded data: 4 skill quests (Mining I, Fishing I, Woodcutting I, Smithing I) + 3 guild quests. If the milestones section shows e.g. \"Dedicated 5 quests\" ✓, the computation used all 7 records ✓. So correct.\n\nBUT the Achivements display shows... hmm, nothing numeric. \n\nOK, alternative: maybe the \"milestones\" are the *Infinite Tower milestones* and the seeded data (tower bonuses) proves claims; the tower screen shows them locked. That's a bug consistent with \"progress toward milestones computed from all finished progress records\" (finished floor records). The tower screen is reachable from the profile? No, but the Achievements TOWER group is on the profile.\n\nHmm, let me look at the Achievements TOWER group again and consider whether \"First Step\" should be ✓. The tower screen says Floor 1 and \"Attempt Floor 1\". If the player has never cleared a floor, they couldn't have earned tower bonuses. Since the developer confirmed the bonuses are earned, the tower progress state must be >0, so the achievements and tower screen are inconsistent → bug. This seems like a genuine, checkable contradiction. But is it the injected bug? Possibly the bug is in the *milestone progress computation* indeed.\n\nBut wait, the tower screen's milestone list shows \"Floor 10\" labels (locked). If the player's best floor were 260, the milestone buttons for floors 10..250 would be claimable/claimed. The buttons are disabled — maybe because they're claimed (claimed = disabled!). And the \"Tower Legend: Claim all 25\" achievement would be ✓ if all 25 claimed. It's ✗. If not all claimed (e.g., 12+3+...), the remaining unclaimed milestones could be at floor 270+ — and their buttons would be... disabled too? Hmm, we'd expect unclaimed-but-reached to be enabled (\"Claim\"). All are disabled. Hmm.\n\nThe tower's top says \"Floor 1\" — if milestones were claimed, the player's next floor would be higher. So floor progress = 0 seems likely, meaning the tower bonuses were granted without floor progress → data inconsistency.\n\nI think reporting this as a milestone-progress bug is risky (it may be intended seeded state where bonuses are aggregate without floor progress). The developer confirmed the bonuses issue; maybe the reply could hint.\n\nLet me think about what else to verify in the areas:\n- \"Profile milestones section\": maybe I should look at the *Pets* section's \"0 / 30 obtained\" and *Armory* \"16 / 367\" and *Bestiary* \"0/100\" — these are \"progress\" but not milestones.\n- The profile header \"Total Level 720\" etc.\n\nHmm, maybe the \"milestones\" section IS the \"Achievements\" (13/38). Let me test it for correctness: \"13 / 38 obtained 34%\" — count 13 ✓ (I counted). 13/38 = 34.2% ✓. Individual obtained states all consistent with data EXCEPT the tower ones if bonuses imply floors. Hmm.\n\nActually, hold on! Let me reconsider the tower achievements given the confirmed bonuses. The developer confirmed that the profile has earned Infinite Tower bonuses (+7% XP, +12% coin drops, +150 HP). Those bonuses are granted by claiming tower milestones (the only source of such bonuses). Claiming a milestone requires reaching its floor. So the player has cleared many tower floors. Therefore:\n- \"First Step: Clear your first Infinite Tower floor\" MUST be obtained → currently not.\n- \"Tower Initiate: Reach floor 10\" → must be obtained → currently not.\n- \"Void Conqueror: Reach floor 250\" → the +7% XP requires floors 20 + 70 (+2%) + 120? etc. Actually +7% XP could be 1+2+4? or many +1% milestones. Let me see the milestone rewards pattern: Floor 20 +1% XP, Floor 70 +2% XP; maybe Floor 120 +?; likely +7% could be reached by floor ~200. +12% coin drops from 12 × \"+1% tower coin drops\" milestones (floors 110, 160, 210, ... up to ~660) — that would mean very high floors (~660). Hmm, +150 HP = 3 × +50 max HP (floors 60, 160, 260...). So the player's best floor could be ~700+. Then \"Void Conqueror (floor 250)\" must be ✓.\n\nSo the achievements TOWER group being all uncompleted is definitely a contradiction with the confirmed earned bonuses. This is likely a real bug (milestone progress not computed from records!). And it ties to the changed item #1: \"progress toward mission milestones is now computed from all finished progress records.\" Maybe the TOWER achievements are literally \"milestones\"?! \"Tower Legend: Claim all 25 tower milestones\" — the section is about milestones!\n\nHmm, but the phrase \"mission milestones\" — maybe it's a paraphrasing of \"milestones\" (of the tower mission). The \"Profile milestones section\" might be the TOWER achievements group in the Profile's Achievements screen. Hmm, that's a stretch, but the data contradiction is strong.\n\nAlternatively, the \"Milestones\" section in the Infinite Tower screen is the \"profile milestones section\"?? The tower screen is not profile.\n\nGiven the strong data contradiction, let me file a report about the tower milestones/achievements not reflecting earned progress. Which screen/element? The Infinite Tower screen's Milestones section: \"Floor 10\", \"Tower Ring...\" buttons disabled. Expected: milestones for floors already cleared should be claimed/claimable. But this screen isn't in the sweep areas. Hmm, but the Achievements group is on the profile screen.\n\nBetter: file on Profile → Achievements → TOWER group: \"First Step – Clear your first Infinite Tower floor\" not obtained, whil", "truncated": true}
