{"type": "thinking", "text": "Fishing Guild: Shrimp Haul Completed ✓. So completed guild quests: Copper Run ✓, Shrimp Haul ✓ = 2. Iron Quota ✗ (Requires Guild Level 1). Plus skill quests: Fishing I ✓, Mining I ✓, Woodcutting I ✓ = 3; Smithing I ✗ (not completed in UI). Total completed = 5. \n\n\"Dedicated (Complete 5 quests)\" ✓ — exactly 5 if counting both skill and guild quests. So the achievement is consistent with the *app's* records (5). If the app counted only skill quests, it'd be 3 (not achieved). So the achievements count all progress records (guild quests included) → the change fix works.\n\nHmm, but the precondition says Smithing I completed and Iron Quota completed → expected 7. The app shows 5. Could be a data seeding issue or a bug where Smithing I/Iron Quota records are missing. Since the precondition is ground truth, the app is missing those completions → a bug! But where? The Quests screens show Smithing I not completed and Iron Quota requiring guild level 1. Hmm, maybe those two quests were intentionally not completed because the guild level/quest chain doesn't allow it — the precondition might be aspirational data (the sweep's given data) that the app should match. If it doesn't match, it's a data inconsistency. But which screen to report? The Quests → Crafting Skills Smithing I row is out of the sweep area. Hmm.\n\nActually, maybe the precondition's \"Quests completed\" list was used to seed the *progress records* for the milestone test — and the app's achievement \"Dedicated\" (5) would then be wrong if it should be 7 — but 5 achieved is the same either way (≥5). The next milestone is 25. So can't distinguish.\n\nHmm! Unless there's a milestone like \"Complete 3 guild quests\" that should be achieved (3 guild quests completed per precondition) but isn't shown somewhere. Where would that be? The Guild achievements? There are no GUILD achievement groups. Hmm! The Achievements groups: LEVELLING, COMBAT, QUESTS, COLLECTION, PRESTIGE, TOWN, TOWER. No GUILD group. So no guild milestone achievement.\n\nHmm, so \"3 guild quests\" in the precondition is for... the guild level? Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe \"progress toward mission milestones\" refers to a *Guild Hall* milestone: \"Complete 0/2 daily requests to advance\" — no.\n\nHmm, hold on. What about the **\"Banners\"**? no.\n\nLet me look at the whole Achievements list (38 items) again: the groups are LEVELLING (7), COMBAT (6), QUESTS (5), COLLECTION (2), PRESTIGE (6), TOWN (4), TOWER (6) = 36. Hmm, 7+6+5+2+6+4+6 = 36, but 38 total. Maybe LEVELLING has 8 and COMBAT 7? Let me recount from observations:\nLEVELLING: Adventurer, Journeyman, Seasoned, Veteran, Master, Legend, Champion, First Mastery, Completionist = 9.\nCOMBAT: Fighter, Warrior, Champion, Elite, Hero, Max Combat = 6.\nQUESTS: Quester, Dedicated, Quest Hound, Quest Master, Quest Champion = 5.\nCOLLECTION: Animal Friend, Menagerie = 2.\nPRESTIGE: First Reset, Branching Out, End of the Line, Clean Slate, Mastered, True Prestige = 6.\nTOWN: First Renovation, Town Improver, Master Builder, Town of Legend = 4.\nTOWER: First Step, Tower Initiate, Climbing Higher, Century Climber, Void Conqueror, Tower Legend = 6.\nTotal = 9+6+5+2+6+4+6 = 38 ✓.\n\nNo GUILD milestones.\n\nOK so \"mission milestones\" ≠ achievements quests.\n\nHmm, what about \"TOWN\" — the town buildings' upgrades? The Grand Monument is empty; no town upgrades. Hmm, \"First Renovation\" not ✓. Consistent.\n\nNow, let me revisit the \"progress toward mission milestones\" phrase with the *guild quests* data: 3 guild quests completed. The guild quest chain has \"Requires Guild Level N\" gating. The guild level = 0 with \"0/2 dailies\". The guild quest chain's progression (Copper Run completed → Iron Quota requires level 1) — if the player completed Iron Quota and Shrimp Haul per precondition, then... the guild quest *milestones* (completed quests) are not reflected: Iron Quota shows \"Requires Guild Level 1\" (not completed). So the guild's quest milestone progress may be broken! Hmm, but that's in the Guild Hall, and it's about the quest gating, not milestones.\n\nMaybe the precondition's guild quest data points at a *guild quest milestone* feature: e.g., completing all 3 guild quests unlocks something. Hmm.\n\nUgh, I've spent a LOT. Let me now do a final check on the most promising remaining candidates and file:\n\n(A) Tabs layout missing Bonuses/Banners: Let me quickly reproduce: Settings → Tabs → Profile → check tabs (need to confirm no Bonuses/Banners). Then revert to Rail. I've already done this once (reproduced twice). I'll file it, as it's a profile-screen bug with clear expected behavior (feature parity). Hmm, but is it \"intended\"? A profile settings option that removes two sections seems like a bug. The developer reply will tell.\n\n(B) The Fishing/Woodcutting training header missing \"~60/session\" line: file? Probably weak.\n\n(C) Landscape clipping: file? Maybe.\n\nActually — wait! Let me reconsider (B): In the Mining Choose Activity sheet, the header shows \"Session: 56m\" and \"~60 ores/session\". In Fishing's sheet, \"~60 fish/session\" is missing. In Woodcutting's sheet, \"~60 logs/session\" missing. Since the row XP amounts are computed as 60 × per-unit XP, the per-session yield is 60 for all. The missing line is likely a bug but cosmetic. Hmm.\n\nHmm, hold on, maybe the missing line for Fishing/Woodcutting is because those skills are *not* mining? No...\n\nLet me look at the Fishing sheet again: it shows \"Session: 56m\" then divider. Whereas Mining shows \"Session: 56m\" then \"~60 ores/session\" then divider. Maybe the second line only appears if the skill's actions all have the same yield? Hmm.\n\nI could report: \"Skill training screen for Fishing (and Woodcutting) is missing the '~60 fish/session' yield line that Mining shows\". Expected? It's a UI inconsistency. Hmm. Risky.\n\nLet me think about what else could be a deliberate seeded bug in the *skill training* area:\n- The XP bar (verified correct).\n- The action list order (verified correct).\n- The per-session XP previews (\"+720 XP → Level X\") — maybe these are wrong for some skills? Let's verify: Smithing action rows showed no XP preview; Cooking none. Mining showed \"+1,080 XP\" etc. Fishing showed \"+300 XP\" ... \"+2,700 XP → Level 31\". Woodcutting: \"+4,080 XP → Level 32\" for Willow Logs (68 XP/log × 60 = 4,080). Woodcutting level 30 XP 13,363; +4,080 = 17,443. Level 32 requires 16,456, level 33 requires 18,247 → so after +4,080 the level is 32 ✓ (\"→ Level 32\"). ✓ correct.\n\n- The \"Owned\" counts in the action list: Copper Ore \"Owned: 40\" ✓ (precondition 40; unchanged since no session used copper). Tin 25 ✓. Stone \"Owned: 12\" — BUT I just completed a Stone session which should have ADDED 60 Stone → inventory should be 72! Let me check! Earlier, after the session, the Skills tab showed Mining XP 102,053. The action sheet showed Stone \"Owned: 12\" BEFORE the session. After collecting (Stone ×60), the Owned count should be 72. Let me check the Mining sheet now: Stone Owned? That tests state persistence (inventory update after session collect). If it still shows 12, that's a bug (collect didn't add loot)! Let me check Inventory too (should show Stone ×72 and Sapphire ×1).\n\nThat's a great state test! Let me open the Mining Choose Activity and check \"Owned: 12\" for Stone."}
