{"type": "thinking", "text": "Rail restored. Settings back to original (Rail, other settings unchanged).\n\nNow, remaining areas to check before sign-off:\n- Profile milestones: I haven't found a dedicated section; the tower milestone issue is already logged. Hmm.\n- Skill training: XP bar and action list look correct.\n\nLet me consider the possibility that the \"profile milestones section\" is in the Achievements screen and its progress numbers are displayed via the *header* (\"13/38\"). If the bug is that some achievements are wrongly marked, the tower ones (already logged) may be it.\n\nHmm, but the developer said \"that one is already logged\" for the tower milestone progress. So it's a known issue, likely the same seeded bug (the sweep's milestones item). OK.\n\nGiven that, maybe the sweep's remaining bug is in the skill training area and I should look harder. Let me re-examine the training screen data:\n\n1. Mining Choose Activity: Rune Essence \"Lv. 1 • 15 XP/ore\" \"Owned: 0\" \"+900 XP\"; Copper \"Lv. 1 • 18 XP/ore\" \"Owned: 40\" \"+1,080 XP\"; Tin \"Lv. 1\" \"+1,080\"; Stone \"Lv. 10 • 12 XP/ore\" \"+720\"; Iron \"Lv. 15 • 35\" \"+2,100\"; Silver \"Lv. 20 • 40\" \"+2,400\"; Coal \"Lv. 30 • 50\" \"+3,000\"; Gold \"Lv. 40 • 65\" \"+3,900\". \n\nWait: The \"~60 ores/session\" × XP/ore values are correct. But hold on — Iron Ore shows \"+2,100 XP\" while its row earlier showed \"Lv. 15 • 35 XP/ore\". 60×35 = 2,100 ✓.\n\n2. Notice: The Mining list displays \"Rune Essence\" first; but in the profile Mining detail list, the order was also Rune Essence, Copper, Tin... ✓.\n\n3. Fishing: \"+300, +600, +900, +1,200, +1,800, +2,700\" ✓.\n\n4. The \"→ Level X\" previews: Fishing \"+1,800 XP → Level 31\" and \"+2,700 XP → Level 31\" ✓; Woodcutting \"+4,080 XP → Level 32\" ✓; Mining (0% at level start) showed no \"→ Level\" (correct since +900 from 101,333 = 102,233 < 111,945).\n\nHmm, everything correct.\n\n5. What about the session completion summary: \"XP gained +720 XP\", \"Loot Stone ×60, Sapphire ×1\" ✓ and the XP applied ✓, inventory ✓.\n\n6. What about the \"Session: 56m\" — the session duration. The session summary said \"Time elapsed 56m 7s\" though I shortened it with Debug Finish Now — irrelevant.\n\n7. The Skills tab row after training showed \"Training\" then \"Session Complete!\" etc. ✓.\n\n8. The *queue*: precondition says queue empty. I added one action (Stone) and it started a session immediately. Hmm, \"Add to Session Queue\" vs \"Start Session\" — the label changes when a session is active. Fine.\n\nSo the skill training area seems bug-free in my checks. The only issue I noticed: Fishing/Woodcutting training header missing the \"~60 fish/session\"/\"~60 logs/session\" line that Mining has. Let me verify this is a real inconsistency by checking Woodcutting's sheet screenshot (it showed only \"Session: 56m\" per observation). And Smithing/Cooking are crafting (no yield line). So for gathering skills, Mining shows a yield line; Fishing and Woodcutting don't. Is this a bug? It could be intentional: mining yields *ores* (60), fishing yields *fish* (60), woodcutting yields *logs* (60). Hmm, all should show.\n\nHmm, but maybe the difference is due to the *sheet's* scroll position (the yield line could be above, hidden). The Mining sheet's header: \"Choose Activity\" (y=180), description (255), Quests/Skill Tree (351), \"Session: 56m\" (434), \"~60 ores/session\" (481). The Fishing sheet: \"Choose Activity\" (508), desc (583), Quests/Skill Tree (679), \"Session: 56m\" (762) — then the list starts at 922. There's space for the yield line around 810, but it's absent. The screenshot confirmed absence. So yes, Fishing's sheet lacks the line.\n\nIs that a bug worth reporting? The change list doesn't mention it. It might be pre-existing/intentional (maybe only Mining has multiple yields?). Hmm, wait: Mining's shield: \"~60 ores/session\" — maybe the line shows the *lowest* action... Hmm.\n\nI'll consider reporting it as a minor inconsistency: \"Fishing skill training screen is missing the per-session yield line ('~60 fish/session') that Mining's shows; users can't see how many fish a session yields.\" Symptom: missing. Evidence: Mining sheet \"~60 ores/session\" vs Fishing sheet lacking. Hmm, comparing across screens is weak for a report on Fishing. But it is a \"consistency\" check which the task encourages.\n\nRisk: rejected. Hmm.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the \"~60 ores/session\" line is a *new* addition only for mining while Fishing/Woodcutting are the bug (missing). Could be.\n\nLet me also check one more *profile* thing I noticed: In the Profile → Skills grid, the Mercantile tile at level 99 had a *full gold ring*. With Mercantile XP unknown; if not max, wrong. Also \"Mercantile Cape\" exists in inventory (granted at 99). Fine.\n\nAnd the Total Level 720 vs sum of displayed levels: let me verify with the actual levels from the profile (Combat 70,70,70,40,40,70; Mining 50; Fishing 30; WC 30; Farming 1; Thieving 1; Smithing 19; Cooking 25; Fletching 1; Crafting 20; Runecrafting ?; Herblore ?; Firemaking ?; Construction ?; Prayer 45; Mercantile 99; Agility 20; Slayer ?). I can compute if I know the unknown levels. Earlier I derived Construction 14 from -7%, and the unknowns (Runecrafting/Herblore/Firemaking/Slayer) probably 1 each except Slayer. Let's compute: Sum known = 360 + (50+30+30+1+1=112) + (19+25+1+20+14=79) + (45+99+20=164) = 715. + Runecrafting1 + Herblore1 + Firemaking1 = 718 + Slayer = 720 → Slayer 2. But the Slayer screen showed \"Slayer Level 1\" with \"0 XP\". Hmm! 718 + 1 = 719, not 720. So either Construction is 15 (→ -7.5%) or one of the craft skills is 2, or Slayer counts... \n\nHmm, the Slayer Master screen showed \"Level 1\" and the profile Slayer tile? The profile grid had \"Slayer\" with debug button; level unknown (maybe 2?). The Slayer screen's top said \"Slayer / Level 1 / 0 XP\". Hmm, that's the *Slayer* skill level 1 with 0 XP. So Total Level would be 719, not 720 — a 1-level discrepancy! Interesting. Unless Construction is 15 (then -7.5%, rounded/truncated to -7%). Then total = 720 ✓ and the bonus \"-7%\" would be a rounding of 7.5%... Hmm, which is right?\n\nLet me verify Construction's level directly. If Construction is 15 and the bonus shows -7% (expected -7.5%), that could be a *bug* in the bonus value (wrong_value)! Or if Construction is 14 and total level is 719 (bug in total level). Hmm!\n\nLet me check Construction's level via the Profile → Skills grid tile. I need to scroll to the CRAFTING section and read the Construction tile's level circle. Alternatively tap the Construction tile → detail sheet shows \"Level X\"! That's quick-ish: Profile → Skills → scroll ~4 swipes → tap Construction tile (element ~685,1701) → read \"Level X\".\n\nLet me do it. This could reveal a bonus value bug (in my area!)."}
