nI think I've thoroughly tested the skill training screens. \n\nLet me do a last check on the *profile milestones*: maybe it's the \"Achievements\" progress and I should compare the count with a fuller computation. We counted 13 obtained. Let me verify each obtained achievement against the data:\n- Adventurer (total 50) ✓, Journeyman (100) ✓, Seasoned (250) ✓, Veteran (500) ✓ — total 720 ✓.\n- Master (750) ✗ ✓ correct.\n- First Mastery (any 99) ✓ — Mercantile 99 ✓.\n- Completionist ✗ ✓.\n- Fighter (combat 10) ✓, Warrior (30) ✓, Champion (50) ✓, Elite (75) ✓ — combat 80 ✓.\n- Hero (99) ✗ ✓.\n- Max Combat (113) ✗ ✓.\n- Quester (1 quest) ✓, Dedicated (5 quests) ✓ — app has 5 completed ✓ (3 skill + 2 guild), consistent.\n- Quest Hound (25) ✗ ✓.\n- Animal Friend (first pet) ✗ ✓ (0 pets).\n- First Reset (prestige any) ✓ — Attack/HP prestiged ✓.\n- Branching Out (first tree upgrade) ✓ — Precision/Vitality owned ✓.\n- End of the Line ✗ (not all in one path) — Precision I+II = 2 of 5? ✗ correct.\n- Clean Slate ✗, Mastered ✗, True Prestige ✗ ✓.\n- TOWN all ✗ — no town upgrades ✓ (Grand Monument empty; buildings tier 0 ✓).\n- TOWER all ✗ — contradicts tower bonuses (reported, already logged).\n\nSo achievements are consistent except TOWER. Fine.\n\nSo the only remaining issue is the tower milestones (known) — and maybe the \"milestones section\" = Achievements' TOWER progress (same root). So I've covered it.\n\nWait — maybe I should double check the *\"Missing\" filter count* / \"All\" toggles for state bugs? Not needed.\n\nOne more idea for \"profile milestones\": maybe the \"milestones\" are the **Pets' collection milestones** (0/30) and the bug is that the pet progress should reflect... no pets.\n\nOK, let me also verify the profile screen's other sections quickly for obvious wrong data vs preconditions:\n- Inventory: counts match mostly (Stone 72 after my session, Sapphire x1 new, Mercantile Cape extra). Hmm! Mercantile Cape ×1 — the precondition inventory didn't list it. Is that a bug? A \"Mercantile Cape\" might be auto-granted for reaching level 99, so the precondition list may omit it. Hmm, but the precondition inventory list is explicit: \"Inventory: Bronze Pickaxe x1, Bronze Axe x2, ... Wool x7.\" No Mercantile Cape. So the inventory has an extra item not in the preconditions. Hmm! That could indicate a bug (e.g., duplicate/extra item). But it might be intended as a level-99 reward (cape). The precondition says \"Mercantile level 99\" — a cape for 99 is plausible. The precondition's inventory list might be incomplete... Risky.\n\nHmm, also I added Sapphire ×1 and +60 Stone via the session, so the inventory now differs from the precondition due to my testing — expected.\n\n- Gear: equipped items match (Bronze Pickaxe, Axe, Fishing Rod; Iron Sword; Bronze Boots). ✓\n- Achievements: 13/38 ✓.\n- Pets: 0/30 ✓.\n- Armory: 16/367.\n- Bestiary: 0/100.\n- Banners: two unobtained.\n- Bonuses: missing tower bonuses (logged).\n\nOK. I think I can sign off now — but wait, the task might expect finding the XP bar/action list bug if one exists. I verified they're correct. Signing off is appropriate if no remaining bugs in areas.\n\nHmm, but the \"worst outcome\" is signing off with bugs. Let me do a couple of final high-value checks in the skill training area:\n\n1. Skill Tree screen for a skill — the \"Prestige\" node states and \"Reach level 99 to prestige (currently 50)\" — a consistency check: Mining level 50 but the profile ring shows 50 ✓. Also the tree says 0 points available, 0 of 25 lifetime points earned. With Attack/HP prestiged once each, lifetime points should be 2 (1 per prestige?)! Hmm! Let me check the Attack skill tree: \"0 points available / 0 of 25 lifetime points earned\"? We saw the *Mining* tree: \"0 of 25 lifetime points earned\" — Mining hasn't prestiged, so 0. But Attack/HP prestiged once each → their trees should have 1 point each (and Precision I+II+Vitality I purchased would consume points: Attack Precision I (1) +